From: RocksDB z/OS Port <zopen@rocksdb>
Date: 2025-01-01
Subject: [PATCH 5b/9] z/OS: include zos_compat.h and tag all data-file fds binary

Include the z/OS compat header (added in patch 5a) early in both env
files so O_DIRECT, O_DIRECTORY, fread_unlocked, major, and minor stubs
are available before any Linux-specific use of those identifiers.

Also tag every data-file fd as CCSID 819 (ISO-8859-1/ASCII) immediately
after open() succeeds. On z/OS with -fzos-le-char-mode=ascii, untagged
files are subject to auto-conversion: the kernel silently translates
between ASCII and EBCDIC on every read/write. RocksDB uses raw
pread/pwrite for all database files (SST, WAL, MANIFEST, CURRENT,
IDENTITY); any auto-conversion corrupts the binary record format,
causing ldb scan to return nothing.
CCSID 819 = ISO-8859-1 = ASCII: correct for files written by an
ASCII-mode process. CCSID 65535 (raw binary) also prevents conversion
but causes ldb and display tools to misread the files.
ZOS_TAG_FD_BINARY calls __chgfdccsid(fd, 819) — a T-symbol in
libzoslib.a. On all other platforms it is a no-op.

